/* Panel de info */
"What is Decruft" = "Qué es Decruft";
"Decruft frees disk space by deleting the folders your dev tools regenerate on their own: dependencies, builds, caches and virtual environments. It scans your project folders, shows how much each one takes and how long its project has been inactive, and lets you delete them manually or automatically every day for idle projects. Nothing it deletes is lost: it comes back with npm install or your next build." = "Decruft libera espacio en disco borrando las carpetas que las herramientas de desarrollo regeneran solas: dependencias, builds, cachés y entornos virtuales. Escanea tus directorios de proyectos, muestra cuánto ocupa cada carpeta y cuántos días lleva inactivo su proyecto, y te deja borrarlas a mano o automáticamente cada día en proyectos parados. Nada de lo que borra se pierde: se recupera con npm install o el siguiente build.";
"What it detects and deletes" = "Qué detecta y borra";
"Always (regenerable by name)" = "Se borran siempre (regenerables por su nombre)";
"Only if they are a real virtualenv (contain pyvenv.cfg)" = "Solo si son un virtualenv real (contienen pyvenv.cfg)";
"They regenerate with pip install -r requirements.txt / uv sync." = "Se regeneran con pip install -r requirements.txt / uv sync.";
"Only if the parent is a JS or Android project (package.json / Gradle)" = "Solo si el padre es un proyecto JS o Android (package.json / Gradle)";
"A dist or build in any other context is treated as code and never touched." = "Un dist o build en otro contexto se considera código y no se toca.";
"Never touched" = "Nunca se toca";
"Inside %@ only node_modules is detected: everything else is installed code (WordPress plugins, Composer packages…). .git and .env are never detected: they are not regenerable." = "Dentro de %@ solo se detecta node_modules: el resto es código instalado (plugins de WordPress, paquetes de Composer…). .git y .env no se detectan nunca: no son regenerables.";

